;; wasmc: not from the upstream suite. wasmc's limit of 65536 function
;; types.
;;
;; Type indices are 16-bit in wasmc (the canonical type of a function, the
;; type of a call_indirect in the IR) and in WAMR's AOT format (the type of
;; an imported function), so the decoder rejects a module with more than
;; 65536 types (WASMC_ERR_TOO_MANY_TYPES).
;;
;; The module below has 65537 types: every type but the last is [] -> [],
;; the last (65536) is [i32] -> []. Function 0 has type 65536 and is table
;; element 0; function 1, exported as "call", runs call_indirect (type 0)
;; on element 0, a type mismatch. Without the limit the module compiled:
;; the canonical index of type 65536, truncated to 16 bits, became 0, and
;; call_indirect ran function 0 instead of trapping with "indirect call
;; type mismatch".
;;
;; It is written in binary, as text would be ten times larger.

;; 65537 types: one more than wasmc allows
(assert_invalid
 (module binary
